# File & Directory Organization Rules

## 1. Directory Structure
```
Legado/
├── App/                       # App lifecycle & DI (LegadoApp.swift, AppEnvironment.swift)
├── Core/                      # Low-level primitives (Architecture, Network, ScriptEngine, RuleParser, Utilities)
├── DesignSystem/              # Liquid Glass UI kit (Materials, Components, Theme, Typography)
├── Domain/                    # Pure Swift business entities & UseCases (no UI imports)
│   ├── Model/
│   ├── Repository/
│   └── UseCases/
├── Data/                      # Database (SwiftData/SQLite), Repositories, WebDAV
└── Features/                  # Feature modules (strictly grouped)
    ├── Bookshelf/
    ├── Reader/
    ├── Explore/
    ├── Search/
    ├── BookDetail/
    ├── SourceManage/
    └── Settings/
```

## 2. Feature Creation Checklist
When creating any new feature in `Legado/Features/<FeatureName>/`:
1. `State/<FeatureName>State.swift`: Defines `struct <FeatureName>State: Equatable`.
2. `Intent/<FeatureName>Intent.swift`: Defines `enum <FeatureName>Intent`.
3. `ViewModel/<FeatureName>ViewModel.swift`: Implements MVI business handling.
4. `View/<FeatureName>View.swift`: Pure declarative rendering.

After adding files, run `make generate` and `make format-check`.
